.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The unit passes these from
.Pa /etc/default/creature-mqtt
to
.Ic creature-mqtt bridge :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CREATURE_SERVER_HOST , Ev CREATURE_SERVER_PORT
The Creature Server whose events are bridged.
.It Ev MQTT_HOST , Ev MQTT_PORT
The MQTT broker the events are published to.
.It Ev OTEL_*
OpenTelemetry export (OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS,
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/default/creature-mqtt
Environment for the service. It is required: copy
.Pa /etc/default/creature-mqtt.env.example
and edit it.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/creature-mqtt.service
The unit, enabled on install. Override it with a drop-in in
.Pa /etc/systemd/system/creature-mqtt.service.d/ .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Bridge a local server to a local broker in the foreground:
.Dl creature-mqtt bridge --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --insecure --mqtt-host 127.0.0.1 --mqtt-port 1883
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr creature-cli 1 ,
.Xr creature-agent 8
